# Title: Deletion of Volume Shadow Copies via WMI with PowerShell
# ID: 21ff4ca9-f13a-41ad-b828-0077b2af2e40
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Tim Rauch, Elastic (idea)
# Date: 2022-09-20
# Tags: attack.impact, attack.t1490
# Description: Detects deletion of Windows Volume Shadow Copies with PowerShell code and Get-WMIObject. This technique is used by numerous ransomware families such as Sodinokibi/REvil
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((process.command_line:*.Delete()* OR process.command_line:*Remove-WmiObject* OR process.command_line:*rwmi* OR process.command_line:*Remove-CimInstance* OR process.command_line:*rcim*)) AND ((process.command_line:*Get-WmiObject* OR process.command_line:*gwmi* OR process.command_line:*Get-CimInstance* OR process.command_line:*gcim*)) AND (process.command_line:*Win32_ShadowCopy*))
